mini batch gradient descent though, if you plot progress on your cost function, then it may not decrease on every iteration.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.480
In particular, on every iteration, you're processing some x t,

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:04.280
y t and so if you plot the cost function j t,

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.960
which is computed

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:16.000
using just x t, y t, then it's as if on every iteration you're training on a different

